---
import './figures.css';
---
<figure class="cl-figure" aria-labelledby="global-reads-title">
  <figcaption id="global-reads-title"><span class="cl-number">Figure 4</span> Pay at the write so reference reads can stay nearby</figcaption>
  <div class="cl-panel">
    <p class="cl-label">GLOBAL · order_statuses · healthy, converged system</p>
    <div class="cl-card"><b>Rare reference-data write</b><span>Agreement, propagation and the protocol’s timestamp wait</span></div>
    <div class="cl-arrow">↓ Higher write latency supports up-to-date regional reads</div>
    <div class="cl-three">{['North','West','East'].map(region=><div class="cl-region"><strong>{region} reader</strong><div class="cl-card cl-active"><b>Nearby qualified read</b><span>pending</span><span>paid</span><span>cancelled</span></div></div>)}</div>
    <div class="cl-banner">Stock remains a guarded write in West.</div>
  </div>
  <p class="cl-caption">A documented-behaviour model of the three existing status definitions, assumed frequently read from every region and rarely changed. The repeated lists show the read result, not three voter groups or an actual write trace. No new status, order or payment is introduced.</p>
</figure>
